{
  "note": "Recorded-voice hook AND Lucy's recording checklist. Placeholders stay null as the full id list. Mapped filenames live in `clips`. Isolated phonemes are kid-voice recreations from reference/Starfall/audio/{A-Z}/phoneme.mp3. Picture words, cheers, and nudges are ElevenLabs Flicker. Letter names stay silent placeholders until Bradley records — never ElevenLabs, never isolated-letter TTS. To ship a clip: drop the file in app/audio/, map it here, add it to SHELL in sw.js, and bump VERSION in sw.js + js/version.js.",
  "base": "audio/",
  "recorded": 426,
  "channels": {
    "music": "Quiet playground wander. Loops audio/music-loop.wav on the music bus. Ducks to 16% while voice plays.",
    "sfx": "Short musical UI hits: tap, select, match chord, miss, star, pop, woof, plus a celebrate xylophone. ElevenLabs beds. Independent of voice: mute one, the other keeps going.",
    "voice": "Lucy. The only channel that uses the clips below."
  },
  "contract": {
    "name": "name-<L> — board appear. The letter NAME only. Example: “A!”",
    "phoneme": "phoneme-<L> — letter-choice tap. The SOUND only, NEVER the name. Example: ah / buh / kuh",
    "word": "word-<L>-<id> — picture tap. The picture's word only. Example: “Apple!” Falls back to word-<L> when the per-picture clip is missing.",
    "cheer": "cheer-<n> — after a correct submitted two-tap. Falls back to a single `cheer` clip.",
    "nudge": "nudge-<n> — after a wrong tap. Falls back to a single `nudge` clip."
  },
  "rules": [
    "Three namespaces, three channels: name-* / phoneme-* / word-* never share an id and must never share a FILE. js/audio.js drops a phoneme id that points at that letter's name file, because that is the one mix-up that would say the letter name on a choice tap.",
    "A phoneme clip says the sound. Recording “A” into phoneme-A is a ship-blocker, not a typo.",
    "Resolution order per line: clip if mapped, else silence. Lucy's on-screen line shows either way. Isolated phonemes are never TTS — they are the Starfall-folder recreations.",
    "ElevenLabs speaks whole picture words and the existing cheer/nudge sentences. Isolated phonemes are Starfall files only. Letter names are recordings only — do not generate name-* TTS.",
    "Nothing plays before a user gesture. The giant PLAY button (and the Grown-Ups Test buttons) unlock the speaker; the header mute dots only set prefs.",
    "Keep clips under about 2s. A clip that stalls is let go of after 8s so the music duck cannot stick."
  ],
